  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02. Each has a progress note, and 3 have an addendum for results that arrived during the work (§8).\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005): furosemide changed to 40 mg BID per the signed addendum (mr-t0001). KCl stopped per the summary. Omeprazole kept; inpatient pantoprazole was a formulary substitution and was not ordered. Lisinopril first stayed held (K 5.4 on 10/21). A repeat BMP on 10/23 (K 4.7, Cr 1.21) then arrived, so it was resumed (mr-00072). An unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 BID was not acted on. Task-t0003 is superseded and I couldn't close it: messaged Dr. Okafor (comm-t0026). Notes doc-t0004 and doc-t0019.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004): carvedilol was raised to 12.5 BID per the summary. A signed addendum on 10/23 reversed it (bradycardia), so it is back to 6.25 BID (mr-t0017). Insulin 70/30 and aspirin unchanged. FLAGGED: atorvastatin fills cover about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so no change (comm-t0006). FLAGGED: outside glipizide (Dr. Desai) is not addressed at discharge and was not ordered (comm-t0007). Notes doc-t0008 and doc-t0020.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044): lisinopril resumed after the 10/22 labs (Cr 1.08, K 4.6). K 5.5 on 10/23 then arrived, so it was re-held (§7). PCP task-t0018 is due 10/26. Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged. Notes doc-t0010 and doc-t0021.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069): lisinopril resumed (post-discharge Cr 1.12, K 4.4). Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. Note doc-t0012.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067): metformin stays held. The only creatinine is from the hospital stay, so the post-discharge condition isn't met. PCP task-t0013 is due 10/24, when the BMP is expected. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. Note doc-t0014.\n\nCompleted 4 arrived inbox items (inbox-a0001 to a0004). Unrelated inbox items for other patients were left untouched.",
